jennifer lopez is opening up about a  scary time in her life when she says she  had a panic attack and felt paralyzed in  her latest on the jlo newsletter the  marry me actress recalls the crippling  experience she writes she thought she  was invincible in her late 20s when she  used to get just three to five hours of  sleep a night as her career was  skyrocketing releasing music like her  debut single  [Music]  and movies like 1998's out of sight  opposite george clooney let's get out of  here  jlo explains that one day she was  sitting in a trailer when she completely  froze work was an all-consuming priority  and she let her self-care needs go  completely quote i found myself feeling  physically paralyzed i couldn't see  clearly and then the physical symptoms i  was having started to scare me and the  fear compounded itself as for how she  recovered jen recalls her security guard  picking her up from the trailer and  driving her to a doctor jen told the doc  she thought she was losing her mind and  he told her she needed to make a big  lifestyle change sleep seven to nine  hours a night no caffeine and plenty of  exercise that's when jennifer decided to  prioritize living a healthy and balanced  life you gotta you know live right you  know you eat right and you work out you  know nobody can escape the hard work  that it takes to get results on anything  in life you all of us have to work hard  at it and i definitely do jen says her  philosophy is more pro-living instead of  anti-aging she lifts weights three to  four days a week and does cardio when  she's trying to shed a few extra pounds  physically you know you want to be in  good shape and when it comes to diet jen  is all about moderation here's a pic of  her typical dinner which includes a  balance of healthy dishes she says the  bread and fries are for her twins 14  year old emmy and max although she  admits to picking at those sometimes too  based on the new pics she shared with  her kids and fiance ben affleck jennifer  seems to be glowing from the inside out  i'm  super excited just last month the triple  threat shared this sweet father's day  tribute to ben  this is the best time of my life i love  my career but nothing is more fulfilling  to me than being able to build a family  with someone who i love deeply and who  is just as dedicated to family and and  to each other as we can be and uh i'm  just i feel incredibly blessed of course  the couple got engaged again in april  after previously being engaged from 2002  to 2004. shortly after ben popped the  question the second time around jen  shared these intimate details it was  totally unexpected  my love came in ben came in and he got  down on one knee  and he said some things that i'll never  forget  and then he pulled out a ring  and he said will you marry me  and it was  the most perfect moment as for when  they'll head down the aisle well a  source told e.t and may that they want  to get married soon and are leaning  toward a destination or tropical wedding  the source adds they can't wait to spend  the rest of their lives together forever  happily in love  you
 

